          "explanation": "Authorized cards in the trick are C4 and C9; North holds CQ7, South CK86, and CA has already been played. CQ cannot be beaten by a remaining club. North can then lead C7 toward CK, preserving the retained development route.",
          "quotes": [
            "Win with the queen, then lead dummy’s remaining club toward the king to continue establishing the suit."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision-0007",
      "status": "pass",
      "findings": [
        {
          "dimension": "established_winners",
          "fact": "C7 toward CK draws the sole outstanding club and establishes five club tricks overall.",
          "explanation": "Authorized history records defenders' C3, C5, C9 and CT. With North holding C7 and South CK86, CJ is the only outstanding defender club. CK captures it from either defender, leaving C8 and C6 winners. Five clubs, two diamonds, two hearts and SA total ten.",
          "quotes": [
            "Lead toward the king to draw the last outstanding club, establishing five club tricks and ten tricks overall."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision-0008",
      "status": "pass",
      "findings": [
        {
          "dimension": "inference_and_transport",
          "fact": "West's CJ is established by the visible play, and the ten-trick cashing route is feasible.",
          "explanation": "Authorized history leaves CJ as the only defender club, and East's H2 discard on C7 places it with West. South's CK draws it, followed by C8, C6, DA and HA. North can win the next heart with HK and lead the retained S8 to South's SA; that obvious return entry supports the stated remainder.",
          "quotes": [
            "Win with the club king, drawing West's remaining jack.",
            "Then cash the diamond ace and heart ace, lead a heart to dummy's king, and cash the spade ace when back in South."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision-0009",
      "status": "pass",
      "findings": [
        {
          "dimension": "remaining_route",
          "fact": "C8 is established, and the retained plan has sufficient winners and transport.",
          "explanation": "Authorized history shows CJ falling under CK, with four tricks won. South retains C86, DA, HA and SA; North retains HK and S862. Two club cashes and four side-suit winners yield ten total. After two spade discards, North's remaining spade provides the return from HK to SA.",
          "quotes": [
            "Cash an established club winner, discarding a low spade from dummy. Ten tricks are secure.",
            "cash the spade ace when back in South."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
